{"t": 1794117761.5698225, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Summary\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` treated page numbers as 0-based: it computed `start = number * size`, so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the *second* page even though the API documents pages as 1-based (`?page=1` is the first page).\n\nThis computes the offset from a 1-based page number instead:\n\n```python\nstart = (number - 1) * size\n```\n\n## Testing\n\n- `page(items, 1, 10)` returns the first 10 items\n- `page(items, 2, 10)` returns items 11-20\n- `page(items, 3, 10)` returns the remainder\n- Out-of-range page returns `[]`; empty input returns `[]`\n- `python -m pytest -q` (no test suite present in the repo)\n\nFixes #57", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix pagination: page() should treat page numbers as 1-based (#57)"}, "ok": true}
